Playing naked was, as I expected, quite a challenge.  Well, playing a
naked Nethack character was quite a challenge.  I've never attempted
to ascend a character while *I* was naked.  I'd be worried my wife
would walk in, then I'd be embarrassed and have to explain what the
hell I was doing...

This was a good challenge.  Most of my characters made it past the
first few levels, then died due to my crappy AC at or near Sokoban,
when somewhat harder monsters start appearing.  I had to relearn basic
things, like using wands, prayer, etc. when I need to, and not saving
them for later.  And don't try to get in 1 more hit if 1 more hit
might kill me.  I'd also make some sophomoric mistakes, like a
promising monk who smacked an orc - oops, a cockatrice - running down
a corridor.

Another big problem is MR - obviously GDSM and CoMR are out.  The only
other way to get MR is from artifacts, so I was going to have to wish
for an artifact for the first time since my very first ascension.
(Unless I happened to sac for Magicbane, which I didn't.)

The last big problem is magic cancellation.  Besides cockatrices,
which are a YASD waiting to happen when naked anyway, you have to
worry about things like green slimes, vampires, etc.  They usually
aren't a problem, since you usually have a good MC by the time you
reach them, but they'd be an issue this game.  These guys would have
to be genocided.

I played random characters, rerolling priests, cavewomen, and
sometimes healers, when I didn't feel like playing them.  Looking at
my logfile, Heidi Klum was the 47th naked character I made an attempt
at playing, and the first barbarian.

I didn't take notes early on because of the high casualty rate in the
early game.  But I do remember that on the first turn, Heidi took off
her +0 ring mail, plus any clothes that are implied but not
specifically listed in the inventory, and packed them away in a box by
the upstairs.

DL2 had a small shop.  DL3 had the branch to the mines.  I didn't need
mithril, so I didn't go there.  DL6 had another shop, DL7 the Oracle,
and DL8 the branch to Sokoban and a chaotic altar.  I did need an "oR,
so I went through Soko and got one.

Then I went down through 2 mine levels to Minetown on level 6.  The
altar was cross-aligned.

I set up a stash on DL9, as I had just become burdened.  It was
definitely nice that it was easy to stay unburdened without armor to
weigh you down.

DL11 was a bones level from Hearse.  I tamed Porthos and killed an
elven mummy named Legostein.  Legostein appeared to have been an
elvish ranger, and obviously was killed by a mummy.  He had a boatload
of wands, though none were particularly special, and a very heavy bag,
which I had to abandon next to the upstairs.

DL12 had shop sounds.  Porthos died, probably killed by an aleax.
Seems early for an aleax, but it didn't appear to be a bones level.  I
had to use a /oDig to get away from the aleax though.

I got in trouble on DL13 again, and had to read a ?oTel and wound up
in a small throne room.  Happily, there was nothing difficult there.
But the chest was empty and the throne just made me stupid.  The aleax
wandered in and I was able to finish it off.

Back to DL12, the shop was a HUGE scroll shop.  I snuck my pickaxe in,
put a pit in the entry square, and robbed it.  I'd intended to convert
to chaotic later (though in the end, I didn't), so I had no remorse
over killing Kiltamagh with daggers.  I think I killed some earlier
shopkeepers this way too, to get protection money.

Somewhere around here, after #dip-testing potions, I started quaff-
testing them, and drank what turned out to be a b!oInvis.  It was
before I started taking notes, but it must have been after this shop
if I snuck a pick-axe in.

Then a werejackal made me feverish.  Stupid magic cancellation.  I had
no wolfsbane on me, my god was angry (probably all those murdered
shopkeepers...), and my AC was 10 now, too.  I really thought that
would be the end of me, but I somehow made it back to my stash on DL9
without becoming a jackal.  But I had no wolfsbane there, either.  I
then somehow made it to the altar on DL8.  I'd hoped to use it to
convert to chaotic later, but out of necessity, I converted it,
mollified Crom, and #prayed.  I made some holy water too, since I
could now.

DL14 had the quest portal, which I stumbled into.  DL16 was Rogue.

DL18 had the ghost of m75.  7 apples, a robe, and no body armor
suggested m75 was a monk, killed by a werewolf's summoned bretheren.
Lots of stuff, but nothing great.

Time for a stash run.  I killed an aleax with Sunsword on the way up.
Damn, now I'd have to wish up my MR artifact before I could sac for a
decent weapon - at least, if I want to be guaranteed to get the wish.
Since I had holy water now, I looted Legostein's bag on the way up.
Nothing of note in there either.  I gained XL14 from a wraith corpse.

DL19 had a small throne room, which did nothing.  I looted a box on
the level and accidentally pick up a heavy gray stone, but it let me
drop it for some reason.  Kick-test confirmed a loadstone. :S

DL20 had a huge beehive, DL21 a small zoo, DL22 another chaotic altar
and a graveyard.  I lost 2 XL to a vampire, gaining 1 back.  I
converted a lawful altar on DL23.

DL25 was the titan version of medusa.  Ugh.  I read a b?oEarth and
killed a summoning storm, but the titan was MIA.  I returned to DL22
to set up a stash by the altar and downstairs, and continued down.

DL26 was a maze.  I found the titan again.  A summoned green slime
slimed me - I hadn't found a /oFire yet(!), and had no !oOil or ?oFire
on me, so I had to #pray.  Happily, another monster took it out while
I was praying (I'd been wearing a =3DoConflict for awhile).  I killed
the titan with the !oParal =3DoFA trick.

I'm wondering how the titan got there though.  I'm pretty sure it's
the same one from Medusa - I didn't find a corpse at Medusa, so I
don't think something killed it due to conflict.  I didn't find a
hole.  I don't think it could have teleported and dug a hole, since
Medusa is no-teleport...  What could have happened?

Anyway, DL27 was another maze.  I stupidly let a minotaur get me all
the way to single-digit HPs, and had to quaff a !oFH.  That was TOO
close!!  DL28 was yet another maze.  I got into trouble again and read
a ?oTel, and ended up right by the downstairs, so I decended.

DL29 was the castle, but I forgot my damn harp in my stash.  I use a
c?oTel to get up past medusa.  Turned out it was all the way up in my
DL9 stash.  I consolidated most of the stash to DL22 while I was
there.

Conflict thinned the horde, and the drawbridge killed most of the
nasties.  I paralyzed another titan who slipped through, and
teleported away a slime that the titan summoned.

The throne gave a wish!  bgfPYEC, please!  I got the /oW and returned
to my stash, and found that the /oW was full.  I wished for 3
bgf?oGeno, wrote a few more (I had 3 markers at this point), and had a
big geno-fest: bye-bye c, L, h, P, ;, R, and V.

Next, I wished for the Orb of Weight.  That 1/2-damage would be nice
later.  Hmm... It would be incredibly difficult to ascend a naked
barbarian without wishing up an artifact that grants MR, but maybe the
Orb was a crutch I didn't need.  I had a monk who ended up on astral
with like a -9 AC, and he ascended largely because he picked the right
altar first.  But then, that was like my 4th ascension.  I'm older and
(in theory) wiser now, I know more tricks, and might be able to make
it though Astral without the Orb...  Bah, well, I have it now.

I returned to my stash/altar on DL22 and sacced for Cleaver,
Ogresmasher, and eventually, finally, Mjollnir.  Then up to Soko to
nurse-dance, and to the quest, where I got the Heart, Bell, and
another marker.

After clearing the Valley (DL30), I returned to Minetown to donate to
the priest and convert the altar.  Turned out the priest didn't want
his altar converted, so he died.  I never did go below Minetown.

I got lycanthropy again on the way back, this time from a wererat.  I
had wolfsbane, but had accidentally left it in my stash and had to
#pray.  It was probably better to save it though, in case this
happened again in Gehennom.  Happily I didn't lose protection this
time - maybe because wererats are neutral?  I summoned 4 rats (Ron,
Ralph, Randy, and Rhonda the Rats), since I could.

Continuing, Ron got killed, then Ralph showed up as a barbed devil
when whistled.  Eventually, Rhonda and Randy both became trolls.
Turned out there was a poly-trap 2 squares away from the downstairs.
Randy died by the time I got back to the Valley, where I bought a -1
AC.  I nurse-danced and alchemized to 441 HP.

DL32 was Asmodeus, DL33 was Juiblex.  I hit several trap doors in the
first few levels of Gehennom, and by the time I finish Juiblex's
swamp, only Rhonda the troll came when whistled.  On DL35, Rhonda ate
2 chameleons and became a baby yellow dragon, then a Mordor orc.  DL36
was Baalzebub, and Rhonda became an ogre lord.  On DL37, I found my
first wand of slow monster (not important, just odd).  Rhonda died on
DL38, apparently from a fire trap.  The stupid ogre was wielding a
very rusty pickaxe.

Rodney's tower was DL40-42.  I noticed Vlad's entrance on DL38, on the
way up for a stash run.  I got what I needed from Vlad, and got to ID
a few items from the throne, but anything I really wanted to ID was in
my bag.  I had to kill feral Ralph on DL32.

Orcus Town was DL43.  He didn't have a /oDeath...  Perhaps Mojo
destroyed it and I didn't notice?  DL46 had the fake tower with the
portal, and I cleared Rodney's tower except Rodney himself.  DL48 was
the other fake tower, and DL49 the Vibrating Square.

I spent awhile at my stash prepping for Rodney.  Alchemized some more,
wished up 3 more markers (mostly for ID and charging) and ate some
rings for +3 Protection and PfSC.  I ate some tengu tins I'd made -
the first made me jumpy, but 2 more and I was in control.

When I was finally satisfied I was as ready as I was going to be, I
killed Rodney and level-ported to the Sanctum.  I did the trick where
I go back up the stairs and level-port back down.  I got a /oD off a
priest.

The force was moderately annoying.  But I used my one c!oGL to skip
Juiblex, and surprisingly didn't have to do the swamp again.  I got
another /oD off a pony, of all things.  Back to the stash, I did my
final preparations for ascension.  Blessed and quaffed 2 smoky potions
(oil - yuck!) and got a wish!  I figured a /oPoly would be useful on
Air.  Blessed a bunch of stuff, made 5 more !oFH, yadda yadda.  Funny
how even without armor, I still had to pare down my inventory.
Finally, I headed up.

On Earth, Rodney made his obligatory appearance.  He summoned a horde,
which got me down near 300 HP by the end.  But I wasn't worried - this
being Earth, not a lot of monsters could wander over while I cleared
out the small area.  The portal was just 3 zaps away.

For Air, I had just 1 !oPoly and 4 charges on the /oPoly I'd wished
for.  The PYEC added just 2 charges, so I had to burn 2 /oD charges on
air elementals, and fight my way out of a couple more.  And when a
ki-rin surrounded me with a horde, I had to /oTel him away, then break
the wand to remove the horde.  Again, I was never really in danger,
but it made me think I might have been wise to wish up the Orb of
Weight way back at the castle.  But we'll see how sticky things get on
Astral.

On Fire, I had to use 2 !oFH and 2 /oTel charges to fend off 2
archons' summoning storms plus the converging Fire residents.  I'd
really wanted to avoid using any of that until Astral.

Water, at least, was going to be easy with ;s genocided.  And it was,
mostly.  Except that I got hungry, Rodney appeared, and the portal was
a major pain in the butt to find.  But I got there, using a few /oD
charges on Rodney.

I quaffed 7 b!oSpeed, confused myself, and stepped onto Astral.  I was
on the left side near Pesty, with Death straight ahead and Famine to
the right.  While still confused, I read 4 ?oCM and a ?oTaming to get
a buttload of pet acid blobs for a buffer (plus Pat the Pit Viper and
Zeke the Zruty, who were nearby).  I usually go for Famine first and
Pesty last, but I was closer to Pesty and could /oD it, so I went
left. No dice though, it was lawful.

Someone with a /oMM kept wasting my acid blobs, but there were still a
bunch left.  I went center next, ready to wield a !oParal for Death.
But it wasn't necessary.  Death was around back having a smoke, and
this altar was neutral.  I whistled over 7 lucky acid blobs to come
with me (Pat and my guardian angel were dead, and Zeke didn't win the
Adjacent Square Lottery).  Then I got 2 bits for an ale, in case no
one at the ascension bar wants to buy a naked Heidi Klum a drink, and
offered the amulet!

So maybe I could have gotten by without the Orb of Weight.  Who knows?

I didn't think I was especially overprepared, but I could have easily
gone to all 3 altars without a problem.  I suspect it would have been
winnable without the Orb, but it might have been more touch-and-go at
times.  But that's ok, this was a fun game anyway.


